    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas data transfer pricing varies by cloud provider and by the region of the source and destination nodes, and Atlas charges for data transfer between an Atlas node and another node. AWS separates VPC peering traffic that stays within an Availability Zone (free) from traffic that crosses AZs or Regions (charged). AWS peering line items should not be assumed to describe Atlas's internal replication paths. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/data-transfer-costs.md ; https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/demystifying-amazon-vpc-peering-charges/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/data-transfer-costs.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:109965bee1cfc09f1102a0936ded37cdf1992cfbddc64275a28a423494c9748a",
