    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas documents chargeable node-to-node transfers within a cloud region and across regions; one cluster is therefore not a blanket exemption from transfer billing. Multi-region clusters can have higher transfer costs depending on region placement and deployment size. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/data-transfer-costs.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ecf0a85c39b4a7f49a78e202bdd720e787b1e24400001b888d703f1694a82e11",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0dc5e86e0b327cb9366ec6945507f558e668b731d00953e3be656aaf0e0660ed",
            "ev:f45992fe75f9d3bb2fa2f58913118aca67f6e960f206edfc3926f002abbc5da6",
            "ev:f46dd1cb22644a5e612ffa177483c9a2cae07aa22846cdbc43e81c9b7352e9d4"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/cost-saving-config.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas always compresses intra-cluster communication. Enabling driver compression affects the client-server path; it does not newly enable compression for replication traffic already compressed by Atlas. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/data-transfer-costs.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dc29233c06f66d29deac6889ee958e2e6c3f87969005441718fd57d1a487261c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:67775155540cfedb26e28369b21c9c01a8318264b9dbaf4110198b9021db1efd",
            "ev:aa68b10685a1b4604f373442684f4b5964bb9bb60e2484a84c69ab4a0a1c457f"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/cost-saving-config.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "AWS reports cross-AZ VPC peering charges under the usage types VpcPeering-In-Bytes and VpcPeering-Out-Bytes, so it describes both inbound and outbound peering usage. Atlas documents that it does not charge for incoming data transfers to an Atlas cluster. AWS peering rates therefore should not be applied directly to an Atlas invoice. Sources: https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/demystifying-amazon-vpc-peering-charges/ ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/data-transfer-costs.md",
          "source": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/demystifying-amazon-vpc-peering-charges/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:17f728d267b068e673a07adda21068e89d080210f23f7e9789faa4f2945b8cd5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
